<div id="2026-09-11-hdry-traveler-skew-and-crosscheck" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-11 — Traveler hardcoded-origin skew removed + HDRY part-number cross-check doc</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> (1) Removed two hardcoded blocks in <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Manufacturing/Traveler.pm</code> that forced traveler classification away from the truthful <code>item_origin</code>: the leaf-dropping <code>next if $sku =~ /^INT-HDRY-(BBL|...|WHEEL)/i</code> filters (which silently deleted HDRY structural parts from the traveler) and the <code>if ($origin ne '3d_printed' &amp;&amp; $sku =~ /^INT-HDRY-(...|WHEEL)/i) { $origin = '3d_printed' }</code> override (which force-flagged any INT-HDRY* SKU as printed regardless of its real origin). The traveler now trusts <code>item_origin</code> from the inventory item, so purchase vs print vs assembly is accurate. (2) New doc <code>root/Documentation/hdry_partnumber_crosscheck.tt</code> reconciling every HDRY part code across the assembly-manual PDF, the seven 3MF plate exports, the Upgrade-2 ZIP, and the live inventory (114 HDRY/HW SKUs read from :4003), with the group-plate complication explained.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The user wants the traveler accurate; hardcoded SKU lists create drift and hide parts. The cross-check exists because the project has several overlapping part lists (PDF codes, Orca plate objects, ZIP, inventory) and door hinges/handles ship on group plates, making "how many parts" ambiguous. Documenting the reconciliation stops re-deriving it each session.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Method.</strong> PDF part codes via <code>pdftotext</code>; 3MF part names via <code>unzip -p ... Metadata/*.json</code> + <code>3D/3dmodel.model</code> object names (Orca stores geometry as <code>3D/Objects/object_NN.model</code>, names only in JSON); inventory via read-only <code>GET /Inventory/items</code> on :4003 (no DB hand-edit, no credentials used). <code>perl -c</code> on Traveler.pm: syntax OK.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Manufacturing/Traveler.pm</code> (2 blocks removed), <code>root/Documentation/hdry_partnumber_crosscheck.tt</code> (new), this entry. CODER_READY: if a part still mis-classifies, fix the item's <code>item_origin</code> in inventory, not the traveler code.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Open questions flagged in the doc.</strong> Upgrade-2 inner 3MF names unparsed (binary deflate); SBR03 in PDF but not on a parsed plate; REINFORCEMENT not matched to an inventory SKU; wheel composition (2 half-wheels + tire + foot?) unconfirmed; FFL01/FFR01 variant forks (Sensor/no_Sensor, Panel/no_panel) need a single "real" row chosen for the BOM.</p>
</div>
